{"id":28356,"slug":"vernon-florida","title":"Vernon, Florida","year":1981,"country":"United States","duration":56,"spine":752,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28356-vernon-florida","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/3217a6e471ba2f9239cbe6cb398aa02f/dgNduEohOof1NohG0fGVRpPOyb322m_large.jpg","description":"Vernon is a town in the Florida panhandle surrounded by swamps. Here, Errol Morris found the quietly fascinating subjects for the follow-up to his galvanizing debut, Gates of Heaven. As ever humane yet sharply focused, Morris lets his camera subjects pontificate and perambulate the environs of this seemingly unremarkable little community. The result is a strangely philosophical work that cemented its director’s standing as an important figure in American film.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Errol Morris","slug":"errol-morris"}],"cast":[],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Errol Morris","slug":"errol-morris"},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Errol Morris","slug":"errol-morris"},{"role":"Director of photography","person":"Ned Burgess","slug":null},{"role":"Production manager","person":"Rudd Simmons","slug":null},{"role":"Gaffer/Grip","person":"John Thomas","slug":null},{"role":"Production assistants","person":"Alison Hickey","slug":null},{"role":"Production assistants","person":"Barry Mazor","slug":null},{"role":"Editor","person":"Brad Fuller","slug":null},{"role":"Production sound","person":"Maria Heritier","slug":null},{"role":"Sound rerecording","person":"Mel Zelniker","slug":null},{"role":"Assistant editor","person":"Robin Katz","slug":null},{"role":"Negative cutter","person":"Noëlle Penraat","slug":null},{"role":"Coordinating producer","person":"Kathy Kline","slug":null},{"role":"Executive producer","person":"David Loxton","slug":null},{"role":"Special thanks","person":"New Mexico Department of Development","slug":null},{"role":"Special thanks","person":"Mr. and Mrs. J. W. Martin","slug":null}],"pickedBy":[],"rel